{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-submersion-inner-eq","title":"lem:riemannian-submersion-inner-eq","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":730,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#lem:riemannian-submersion-inner-eq","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-submersion]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:submersion-inner]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"lem:riemannian-submersion-inner-eq","line":1147,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[A Riemannian submersion's base metric is the induced form]\n\\label{lem:riemannian-submersion-inner-eq}\n\n\\uses{def:riemannian-submersion, def:submersion-inner}\n\n\n\n\nIf $\\pi:(\\tilde M,\\tilde g)\\to(M,g)$ is a Riemannian submersion, then $g_{\\pi(x)}=\\beta_x$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:riemannian-submersion,def:submersion-inner,lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec}\n\\sketch Apply the submersion identity to the horizontal vectors $L_xu,L_xv$ and use $d\\pi_xL_xu=u$ and $d\\pi_xL_xv=v$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[A Riemannian submersion&#x27;s base metric is the induced form] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7269656d616e6e69616e2d7375626d657273696f6e2d696e6e65722d6571\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-submersion\">↗ def:riemannian-submersion</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asubmersion-inner\">↗ def:submersion-inner</a> <p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi :(\\tilde M,\\tilde g)\\to (M,g)$\">$\\pi :(\\tilde M,\\tilde g)\\to (M,g)$</span> is a Riemannian submersion, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g_{\\pi (x)}=\\beta _x$\">$g_{\\pi (x)}=\\beta _x$</span>.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-submersion\">↗ def:riemannian-submersion</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asubmersion-inner\">↗ def:submersion-inner</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-lift-linear-spec\">↗ lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec</a> \\sketch Apply the submersion identity to the horizontal vectors <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$L_xu,L_xv$\">$L_xu,L_xv$</span> and use <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d\\pi _xL_xu=u$\">$d\\pi _xL_xu=u$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d\\pi _xL_xv=v$\">$d\\pi _xL_xv=v$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:submersion-inner","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-submersion-metric-unique","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-submersion","title":"def:riemannian-submersion","label":"def:riemannian-submersion"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:submersion-inner","title":"def:submersion-inner","label